#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=9 nAlgorithms=5;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree (version dev) - License GPL v3';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1793971331289'; [Fri Nov 06 14:22:11 CET 2026]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[!Dusky dolphin (Lagenorhynchus obscurus) mitochondrial control-region haplotypes from Cassens et al. (2003),
Mol Ecol 12:1781-1792, DOI 10.1046/j.1365-294x.2003.01876.x. A1-A19: Atlantic (Argentina, South Africa), P1-P7: Pacific (Peru).
Distributed as example data with SplitsTree4.]

[
Input:
Dusky dolphin (Lagenorhynchus obscurus) mitochondrial control-region haplotypes from Cassens et al. (2003),
Mol Ecol 12:1781-1792, DOI 10.1046/j.1365-294x.2003.01876.x. A1-A19: Atlantic (Argentina, South Africa), P1-P7: Pacific (Peru).
Distributed as example data with SplitsTree4.

Methods:
Analysis was performed using SplitsTree (version dev)  (Huson and Bryant 2024 ; DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.).
The original input consisted of 36 taxa and 36 DNA sequences of length 60.
The Hamming Distance method (Hamming 1950) was used (default options) so as to obtain a 36 x 36 distance matrix.
The Split Decomposition method (Bandelt & Dress 1992) was used so as to obtain 58 splits, weakly compatible.
The Show Splits method was used (default options) so as to obtain a Split Network visualization.

References:
Bandelt & Dress 1992: HJ Bandelt and AWM Dress. A canonical decomposition theory for metrics on a finite set. Advances in Mathematics, 92:47–105, 1992.
Hamming 1950: Hamming, Richard W. Error detecting and error correcting codes. Bell System Technical Journal. 29 (2): 147-160. MR 0035935, 1950.
Huson and Bryant 2024: DH Huson and D. Bryant, The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods 21(10):1773-1774 2024.
]

